I built the workflow for slot main-C from brief C and saved it. Lint and the situations check found no problems. One chat turn on the platform showed it starts a call.

The opening line came out reworded. The brief requires "Hello, this is the virtual assistant of FB Services. This call is recorded." exactly, but the test said "...FB Services; we record this call." I set the exact sentence in the workflow, so it is probably being changed at speaking time. I did not have time to find or fix the cause.

**How it is built:** The date-facts code step is the start node and leads to the opening. Then come identity, the account lookup (with the account hook as given), a router that states the debt, and a negotiate node for the main path. Each of the six situations you listed has its own node: hardship, dispute, already_paid, transfer, refused and over_limit. Every node that can close sends the call to a final node that says "Thank you for your time. Goodbye." and hangs up.

**Where I differ from the provided facts:**
- **7-day gap:** DATE FACTS has a GAP line saying any two dates promised in the call must be at least 7 days apart. The brief only requires that between the two parts of one two-part plan. I followed the brief and told the model the gap applies only within a plan.
- **Large debts:** the code's deadlines don't apply the brief's rule that arrears of 1,000.00 or more get a 7-day deadline (or less, if the account's own number is smaller). I wrote that rule into the prompts and told the model to look the date up in the calendar. Nothing in code enforces it.

