I made one edit to the workflow. Every other failure came from the test setup, not from the workflow. The file still loads as JSON in python3.

**Root cause:** the persona customers (PUB-13, PUB-02 and the rest) don't exist at the bank. A test call to `verify_identity` with PUB-13 returned `{"ok": false, "error": "unknown customer_id"}`. So every tool call in the selftest was refused, including `close_call` and `schedule_callback`, and nothing reached the ledger (tools: [] in every row). On top of that, the harness gave no postcodes, so the personas made up invalid ones ("12345 AB", "SW1A 1AA", "90210"). The bank rejected those as unreadable, which doesn't count as a wrong answer, so the agent asked for the postcode again and again. The agent's dates also didn't match the persona's date (it offered Sunday, October 12 when the persona's date is October 14), which points to the call time not being passed in either. None of this can be fixed in the workflow, and these personas can't pass on this setup until they use real customers with real postcodes.

The agent also never gives up after repeated unreadable postcodes, so a real customer could get stuck the same way. The brief has no rule for this, so I left it unchanged.

One line per failure:
- **Full card payment, then loan negotiation** (close_call once, create_promise, arranged): ignored. The customer is unknown to the bank, so identity could never pass and every tool call was refused.
- **Two parts agreed, then a longer plan** (close_call, create_promise, transfer to payment_plans, PLAN): ignored, same reason (unknown customer, made-up postcode).
- **Cannot pay, declines breathing space** (close_call, HARDSHIP note, no_payment / HARDSHIP): ignored, same reason.
- **Unverified payment claim** (close_call, PAID_CLAIMED note and code): ignored, same reason.
- **Refuses security, close_call / id_failed / DECLINED:** ignored. The agent did stop asking, but the bank refused `close_call` because the customer is unknown.
- **Refuses security, "account" said before verification:** fixed. Brief rule 17 says to tell the customer "the checks protect their account", which clashes with the rule against mentioning any account before identity is verified. I changed that line in the identity prompt so the agent says "These checks protect you and your details." and never says "account" until identity has passed.
- **Partner corrects an invalid callback day** (close_call, schedule_callback, CALLBACK): ignored. The bank refused the calls (unknown customer), and the wrong dates the agent offered come from the call time not being passed in.

